---
source: packages/parser/tests/spec.rs
expression: parse(&src)
---
meta: ~
body:
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 2
        kind: UnorderedList
    children:
      - kind: Paragraph
        children:
          - kind:
              Text: "title \"Mog Syntax Specification\" authors \"Drake Bott\" version 0.1"
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 1
        kind: Heading
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: Mog Syntax Specification v0.1
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 2
        kind: Heading
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: Introduction
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "Mog is a markup syntax designed for rich, interconnected documents: knowledge bases, wikis, and publishing on the web. It draws from Markdown, Org, and Neorg, but diverges with two-character delimiters, explicit nesting, and inline attributes. Together these create a unified grammar for expression. This document specifies the structure and rules for markup in a Mog document."
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 2
        kind: Heading
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: Table of Contents
  - kind: Table
    children:
      - kind:
          Delimiter: TableHeader
        children:
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: Section
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: Title
      - kind:
          Delimiter: TableRow
        children:
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: "1"
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: Document Structure
      - kind:
          Delimiter: TableRow
        children:
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: "2"
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: Structural Markers
      - kind:
          Delimiter: TableRow
        children:
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: "3"
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: Attributes
      - kind:
          Delimiter: TableRow
        children:
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: "4"
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: Semantic Delimiters
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 2
        kind: Heading
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: 1 Document Structure
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 3
        kind: Heading
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: 1.1 Text Encoding
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "Documents are UTF-8 encoded files with a "
      - kind:
          Delimiter: Verbatim
        children:
          - kind:
              Raw: ".mg"
      - kind:
          Text: " file extension. A leading byte-order mark (U+FEFF) is stripped by the parser and not considered document content. Line endings can be LF (U+000A) or CRLF (U+000D U+000A), parsing normalizes to LF."
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 3
        kind: Heading
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: 1.2 Whitespace
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "The following Unicode characters are considered whitespace:"
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 1
        kind: UnorderedList
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: Tab (0x09)
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 1
        kind: UnorderedList
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: Space (0x20)
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "Whitespace is not used to structure Mog. Leading and trailing whitespace is trimmed when parsing a document. The following headings parse identically:"
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "# My heading"
      - kind:
          Raw: "  # My heading  "
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 3
        kind: Heading
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: 1.3 Paragraphs
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "A paragraph is a continuous sequence of text lines. Paragraphs are terminated by a blank line, structural marker, or the end of the document. Line breaks within a paragraph are parsed as soft wraps."
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 3
        kind: Heading
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: 1.4 Metadata
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "Metadata may appear at the beginning of a document, delimited by two hyphens. Data is formatted in "
      - kind:
          Delimiter: Link
        attributes:
          - value: https
        children:
          - kind:
              Text: //kdl.dev
      - kind:
          Delimiter: LinkName
        children:
          - kind:
              Text: KDL
      - kind:
          Text: " syntax:"
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "--"
      - kind:
          Raw: "title \"My Document\""
      - kind:
          Raw: "authors \"John\" \"Jane\""
      - kind:
          Raw: "date \"2026-04-15\""
      - kind:
          Raw: version 1
      - kind:
          Raw: "--"
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 3
        kind: Heading
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: 1.5 Escape Sequences
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "A backslash immediately preceding a delimiter or structural marker escapes it, rendering the delimiter or marker literal. A backslash in any other position is itself literal and requires no escaping."
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "\\**this is not bold\\**"
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 2
        kind: Heading
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: 2 Structural Markers
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "Structural markers are used to give documents structure. These markers open the line they are used on, ignoring leading whitespace. Structural markers are repeated to explicitly indicate nesting. Using a heading "
      - kind:
          Delimiter: Verbatim
        children:
          - kind:
              Raw: "#"
      - kind:
          Text: " marker once is a top-level heading, two markers "
      - kind:
          Delimiter: Verbatim
        children:
          - kind:
              Raw: "##"
      - kind:
          Text: " represent a subheading and so on. These rules apply to all structural markers."
  - kind: Table
    children:
      - kind:
          Delimiter: TableHeader
        children:
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: Marker
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: AST Node
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: Semantic Meaning
      - kind:
          Delimiter: TableRow
        children:
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Delimiter: Verbatim
                children:
                  - kind:
                      Raw: "#"
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: heading
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: Section heading
      - kind:
          Delimiter: TableRow
        children:
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Delimiter: Verbatim
                children:
                  - kind:
                      Raw: "-"
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: unordered-list
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: Unordered list item
      - kind:
          Delimiter: TableRow
        children:
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Delimiter: Verbatim
                children:
                  - kind:
                      Raw: "."
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: ordered-list
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: Ordered list item
      - kind:
          Delimiter: TableRow
        children:
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Delimiter: Verbatim
                children:
                  - kind:
                      Raw: ">"
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: blockquote
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: Blockquote
      - kind:
          Delimiter: TableRow
        children:
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Delimiter: Verbatim
                children:
                  - kind:
                      Raw: "="
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: thematic-break
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: Thematic break
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: An optional whitespace character can be placed between a marker and content. This whitespace is trimmed when present.
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 3
        kind: Heading
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: 2.1 Nesting
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "All structural markers can nest. Nesting is expressed through marker repetition. A repeated marker indicates a sub-entity:"
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "# Heading 1"
      - kind:
          Raw: "## Heading 2"
      - kind:
          Raw: "### Heading 3"
      - kind:
          Raw: " ## Heading 2 with leading whitespace"
      - kind:
          Raw: "  # Heading 1 with leading whitespace"
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 3
        kind: Heading
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: 2.2 Blocks
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "Structured text can span multiple lines. A structural marker alone on a line with no content opens a block of its type, terminated with a matching marker of the same depth on its own line."
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "- Reading notes"
      - kind:
          Raw: "--"
      - kind:
          Raw: "Chapter 3 was particularly relevant:"
      - kind:
          Raw: " >"
      - kind:
          Raw: "  quote from chapter 3"
      - kind:
          Raw: " >"
      - kind:
          Raw: "--"
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "Leading whitespace is trimmed while parsing structural markers. Authors can use it to visually group text without affecting nesting depth. The following block is equivalent to the above example:"
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "- Reading notes"
      - kind:
          Raw: "--"
      - kind:
          Raw: "Chapter 3 was particularly relevant:"
      - kind:
          Raw: ">"
      - kind:
          Raw: quote from chapter 3
      - kind:
          Raw: ">"
      - kind:
          Raw: "--"
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 3
        kind: Heading
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: 2.3 Tasks
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "A task marker can be placed after any structural marker except "
      - kind:
          Delimiter: Verbatim
        children:
          - kind:
              Raw: "="
      - kind:
          Text: " thematic breaks. Tasks are marked using square brackets: "
      - kind:
          Delimiter: Verbatim
        children:
          - kind:
              Raw: "[ ]"
      - kind:
          Text: ". The status of a task is determined by the character between brackets."
  - kind: Table
    children:
      - kind:
          Delimiter: TableHeader
        children:
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: Marker
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: Status
      - kind:
          Delimiter: TableRow
        children:
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Delimiter: Verbatim
                children:
                  - kind:
                      Raw: "[ ]"
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: Undone
      - kind:
          Delimiter: TableRow
        children:
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Delimiter: Verbatim
                children:
                  - kind:
                      Raw: "[x]"
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: Done
      - kind:
          Delimiter: TableRow
        children:
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Delimiter: Verbatim
                children:
                  - kind:
                      Raw: "[~]"
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: In progress
      - kind:
          Delimiter: TableRow
        children:
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Delimiter: Verbatim
                children:
                  - kind:
                      Raw: "[?]"
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: Uncertain
      - kind:
          Delimiter: TableRow
        children:
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Delimiter: Verbatim
                children:
                  - kind:
                      Raw: "[!]"
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: Urgent
      - kind:
          Delimiter: TableRow
        children:
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Delimiter: Verbatim
                children:
                  - kind:
                      Raw: "[-]"
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: Cancelled
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "- [~] Grocery shopping"
      - kind:
          Raw: "-- [x] Eggs"
      - kind:
          Raw: "-- [~] Milk"
      - kind:
          Raw: "-- [?] Oat or almond?"
      - kind:
          Raw: "- [ ] Clean kitchen"
      - kind:
          Raw: "- [!] Call dentist"
      - kind:
          Raw: "- [-] Return sweater"
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 2
        kind: Heading
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: 3 Attributes
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "Attributes are generic data attached to a marker or delimiter, terminated using a colon. After the colon an optional whitespace character is trimmed if present."
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "Attribute names may contain any character except whitespace and the following reserved characters:"
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 1
        kind: UnorderedList
    children:
      - kind:
          Delimiter: Verbatim
        children:
          - kind:
              Raw: ":"
      - kind:
          Text: " (0x3A)"
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 1
        kind: UnorderedList
    children:
      - kind:
          Delimiter: Verbatim
        children:
          - kind:
              Raw: (
      - kind:
          Text: " (0x28)"
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 1
        kind: UnorderedList
    children:
      - kind:
          Delimiter: Verbatim
        children:
          - kind:
              Raw: )
      - kind:
          Text: " (0x29)"
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 1
        kind: UnorderedList
    children:
      - kind:
          Delimiter: Verbatim
        children:
          - kind:
              Raw: "["
      - kind:
          Text: " (0x5B)"
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 1
        kind: UnorderedList
    children:
      - kind:
          Delimiter: Verbatim
        children:
          - kind:
              Raw: "]"
      - kind:
          Text: " (0x5D)"
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 1
        kind: UnorderedList
    children:
      - kind:
          Delimiter: Verbatim
        children:
          - kind:
              Raw: "{"
      - kind:
          Text: " (0x7B)"
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 1
        kind: UnorderedList
    children:
      - kind:
          Delimiter: Verbatim
        children:
          - kind:
              Raw: "}"
      - kind:
          Text: " (0x7D)"
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 1
        kind: UnorderedList
    children:
      - kind:
          Delimiter: Verbatim
        children:
          - kind:
              Raw: "|"
      - kind:
          Text: " (0x7C)"
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 1
        kind: UnorderedList
    children:
      - kind:
          Delimiter: Verbatim
        children:
          - kind:
              Raw: ;
      - kind:
          Text: " (0x3B)"
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 1
        kind: UnorderedList
    children:
      - kind:
          Delimiter: Verbatim
        children:
          - kind:
              Raw: "\""
      - kind:
          Text: " (0x22)"
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 1
        kind: UnorderedList
    children:
      - kind:
          Delimiter: Verbatim
        children:
          - kind:
              Raw: "'"
      - kind:
          Text: " (0x27)"
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 1
        kind: UnorderedList
    children:
      - kind:
          Delimiter: Verbatim
        children:
          - kind:
              Raw: ","
      - kind:
          Text: " (0x2C)"
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 1
        kind: UnorderedList
    children:
      - kind:
          Delimiter: Verbatim
        children:
          - kind:
              Raw: "~"
      - kind:
          Text: " (0x7E)"
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "All other printable characters, including digits and Unicode letters, are permitted."
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "##red:My Heading"
      - kind:
          Raw: "##red: My Heading"
      - kind:
          Raw: ""
      - kind:
          Raw: "- list item with **red: BOLD** content"
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 3
        kind: Heading
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: 3.1 Attribute Chains
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: Additional attributes are added as a chain beginning from the terminating colon of the prior attribute. Attribute chains must stay on the same line as their parent. A newline or whitespace character marks the beginning of text content.
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "##red:underline: My Heading"
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 3
        kind: Heading
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: 3.2 Data Attributes
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "Where an attribute flag is not enough, attributes can be structured using "
      - kind:
          Delimiter: Link
        attributes:
          - value: https
        children:
          - kind:
              Text: //janet-lang.org
      - kind:
          Delimiter: LinkName
        children:
          - kind:
              Text: Janet
      - kind:
          Text: " table or list syntax."
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "-{:key \"value\"}: Table attribute"
      - kind:
          Raw: "-[\"item 1\" \"item 2\"]: List attribute"
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 2
        kind: Heading
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: 4 Semantic Delimiters
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "Semantic delimiters are used both inline and as blocks. All delimiters open and close with two characters. Delimiters of different kinds can nest, but delimiters cannot nest within themselves. Leading and trailing whitespace is trimmed within semantic delimiters."
  - kind: Table
    children:
      - kind:
          Delimiter: TableHeader
        children:
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: Delimiter
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: AST Node
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: Semantic Meaning
      - kind:
          Delimiter: TableRow
        children:
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Delimiter: Verbatim
                children:
                  - kind:
                      Raw: "**"
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: strong
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: Bold
      - kind:
          Delimiter: TableRow
        children:
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Delimiter: Verbatim
                children:
                  - kind:
                      Raw: __
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: italic
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: Italic
      - kind:
          Delimiter: TableRow
        children:
          - kind:
              Delimiter: TableCell
            children:
