            children:
              - kind:
                  Text: Footnote content
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: The quick brown fox jumped over the **lazy dog.**
      - kind:
          Raw: ""
      - kind:
          Raw: "**"
      - kind:
          Raw: The quick brown fox jumped over the lazy dog.
      - kind:
          Raw: "**"
      - kind:
          Raw: ""
      - kind:
          Raw: A paragraph **with
      - kind:
          Raw: soft wrapping** in
      - kind:
          Raw: it.
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 3
        kind: Heading
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: 4.1 Verbatim
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "Text between verbatim delimiters is preserved literally. To indicate a syntax for highlighting when rendered, a lang attribute is attached to the marker or delimiter."
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "Some code with \\``python: print(\"Hello, world!\")\\``"
      - kind:
          Raw: ""
      - kind:
          Raw: "``python:"
      - kind:
          Raw: "def greet(name):"
      - kind:
          Raw: "    print(f\"Hello, {name}!\")"
      - kind:
          Raw: "``"
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: Each line of a verbatim block is dedented by the whitespace preceding the opening verbatim delimiter.
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "-"
      - kind:
          Raw: "  A list item"
      - kind:
          Raw: "  ``python:"
      - kind:
          Raw: "  def greet(name):"
      - kind:
          Raw: "    print(f\"Hello, {name}!\")"
      - kind:
          Raw: "  ``"
      - kind:
          Raw: "-"
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "When parsed, the verbatim text is dedented:"
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: python
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "def greet(name):"
      - kind:
          Raw: "  print(f\"Hello, {name}!\")"
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 3
        kind: Heading
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: 4.2 Tables
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "Tables are constructed using "
      - kind:
          Delimiter: Verbatim
        children:
          - kind:
              Raw: "#|"
      - kind:
          Text: " table header and "
      - kind:
          Delimiter: Verbatim
        children:
          - kind:
              Raw: "-|"
      - kind:
          Text: " table row delimiters. Within a row, cells are delimited using "
      - kind:
          Delimiter: Verbatim
        children:
          - kind:
              Raw: "||"
      - kind:
          Text: ". Table cells can include semantic delimiters for presentation of tabulated data. A table is terminated by an empty line."
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "#| Name       || Type      || Color    ||"
      - kind:
          Raw: "-| Apple      || Fruit     || Red      ||"
      - kind:
          Raw: "-| **Carrot** || Vegetable || Orange   ||"
      - kind:
          Raw: "-| Blueberry  || Fruit     || Blue     ||"
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: Table rows may share a line.
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "#| Name || Type || Color || -| Banana || Fruit || Yellow ||"
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: Table rows are not required to have the same number of cells. The number of columns in a table is determined by the row with the most cells. Missing cells are parsed as empty. Implementations may warn on row length mismatch.
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "#| Name       || Type      || Color    ||"
      - kind:
          Raw: "-| Apple      || Fruit     ||"
      - kind:
          Raw: "-| Carrot     || Vegetable || Orange   || Crunchy ||"
      - kind:
          Raw: "-| Blueberry  || Fruit     || Blue     ||"
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "Tables may begin without a header:"
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "-| Apple      || Fruit     ||"
      - kind:
          Raw: "-| Carrot     || Vegetable || Orange   || Crunchy ||"
      - kind:
          Raw: "-| Blueberry  || Fruit     || Blue     ||"
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "A table may have multiple or mid-table header rows:"
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "#|            ||           ||          || Texture ||"
      - kind:
          Raw: "#| Name       || Type      || Color    ||"
      - kind:
          Raw: "-| Apple      || Fruit     ||"
      - kind:
          Raw: "-| Blueberry  || Fruit     || Blue     ||"
      - kind:
          Raw: "#| Vegetables ||"
      - kind:
          Raw: "-| Carrot     || Vegetable || Orange   || Crunchy ||"
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 3
        kind: Heading
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: 4.3 Links
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "Links "
      - kind:
          Delimiter: Verbatim
        children:
          - kind:
              Raw: "[[  ]]"
      - kind:
          Text: " are formatted with square brackets. A link can be bare, or it may have a name "
      - kind:
          Delimiter: Verbatim
        children:
          - kind:
              Raw: ((  ))
      - kind:
          Text: " and footnote "
      - kind:
          Delimiter: Verbatim
        children:
          - kind:
              Raw: "{{  }}"
      - kind:
          Text: "."
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "- [[https://kdl.dev]]"
      - kind:
          Raw: "- [[https://kdl.dev]]((KDL))"
      - kind:
          Raw: "- [[https://kdl.dev]]((KDL)){{ A node-based document language }}"
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "Link resolution is driven by attributes. A bare link is a document reference and is resolved against filenames and metadata "
      - kind:
          Delimiter: Verbatim
        children:
          - kind:
              Raw: title
      - kind:
          Text: " fields. Headings can be referenced using the "
      - kind:
          Delimiter: Verbatim
        children:
          - kind:
              Raw: "#"
      - kind:
          Text: " attribute. External targets are identified by their protocol attribute."
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "[[recipe]]               Document reference"
      - kind:
          Raw: "[[#:Ingredients]]        Heading in current document"
      - kind:
          Raw: "[[https://kdl.dev]]      External via protocol attribute"
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "Link transclusion is indicated using the transclude "
      - kind:
          Delimiter: Verbatim
        children:
          - kind:
              Raw: "!"
      - kind:
          Text: " attribute. Transclusion works for both documents and media."
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "[[!:recipe]]       Document Transclusion"
      - kind:
          Raw: "[[!:image.png]]    Image Transclusion"
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 3
        kind: Heading
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: 4.4 Footnotes
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "When footnote contents do not fit inline, they may be linked from elsewhere in the document:"
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: A good marinara starts with San Marzano
      - kind:
          Raw: "[[tomato]]((tomatoes)) and a generous amount"
      - kind:
          Raw: of olive oil.
      - kind:
          Raw: ""
      - kind:
          Raw: "[[tomato]]{{ A fruit not a vegetable }}"
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "Footnotes can appear without a link. If unattached, a footnote is indexed by its position in the document."
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: A good marinara starts with San Marzano
      - kind:
          Raw: "tomato{{ A tomato is a fruit not a vegetable }} and a generous amount"
      - kind:
          Raw: of olive oil.
